course: dictionary
lesson: 2350
title: Crystal: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer chose. Look at «Most gems are minerals that grew as crystals deep in the Earth.» Gems grow as crystals in the ground, so here a crystal is a solid shape that forms naturally.
explain: «Crystal clear» is a different use. Here crystal describes something, so it works like an adjective. The lake «was crystal clear» means you can see right through it. Ask yourself: does a solid shape fit here? If not, look for another meaning.
explain: Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Try «Mangroves push salt out through their leaves, where you can see salt crystals.» The meaning "solid shape with flat sides and sharp edges" fits, so that is the right one.
fact: A crystal is a solid with a regular shape, flat sides and sharp edges, formed naturally.
fact: Salt, sugar, snowflakes and quartz can all form crystals.
fact: Crystal can also mean very clear, high-quality glass, used for glasses and decorations.
fact: «Crystal clear» means completely clear and very easy to see or understand.
fact: Scientists grow crystals from salt, sugar or alum solutions and look at them with a magnifying glass.
exercise: «Most gems are minerals that grew as crystals deep in the Earth.» In this sentence, what is a crystal? | *A solid with flat sides and sharp edges, formed naturally | A glass used for drinking | A kind of tree | A bright light in the sky
exercise: «The water was crystal clear, so we could see every fish.» What does crystal clear mean? | Full of salt | *Completely clear, very easy to see through | Frozen solid | Cloudy and dirty
exercise: Snowflakes are ice crystals. What shape do they usually have? | Round like a ball | Square with no edges | *Six sides | Long and thin like a stick
test: «Ice cream is stirred while freezing so the ice crystals stay tiny.» What are the ice crystals? | Bright lights in the freezer | Clear windows made of glass | *Tiny solid ice shapes | Melted sugar in a pan
test: In «crystal glasses», what kind of crystal is meant? | Tiny snowflakes on the window | A type of ice cube | A solid shape with flat sides | *A very clear, high-quality glass
exam: Which sentence uses crystal as a noun for a solid shape? | «She was crystal clear about the rules.» | «The lake was crystal clear on a sunny morning.» | *«Mangroves push salt out, and you can see salt crystals on their leaves.» | «The water looked crystal clear and calm.»
